      calibration: { status: "UNPROVEN", evidence: "P189 (2026-08-21): the INSTRUMENT exists and is scheduled; the SAMPLE does not. lib/sports/epl/learning-report.mjs computes the model's mean log loss and Brier over the graded ledger AND the market's over exactly the same matches, from the de-vigged price recorded before kickoff. That comparison was previously impossible: the ledger held the model's probabilities and no baseline, so a model improving while still losing to the closing line would have looked like progress. The de-vigged set existed for a moment inside runEplShadow and was discarded; it is now persisted on the PRIVATE forecast row at forecast time, never re-derived later from whatever odds file is on disk — that would compare the model to a price that did not exist when it spoke. A STOPPING RULE is preregistered before any sample exists, so it cannot be adjusted to spare a result: under 30 paired matches NO verdict is issued (figures still reported, text states they support nothing); materially worse is STOP_AND_DEMOTE with an explicit \"do not tune and re-run\"; tracking without beating is NO_MEASURABLE_ADVANTAGE. The report FITS NOTHING and recommends nothing, enforced by a guard — a pass that measures and adjusts together always finds an adjustment that helps, because it scores the fit on the data that produced it. Guards pin the sign convention (negative delta = model ahead; one flip would report losing as winning), that unpriced matches are EXCLUDED rather than scored as market misses, and that both sides average over the same matches. Live: 1 graded, 0 paired, NO_PAIRED_MATCHES / NOT_YET_ASSESSABLE — proven green in CI. UNPROVEN and not promotable by engineering: it needs matches played. UPDATE (2026-08-24): ADJUDICATED AGAINST THE LIVE ARTIFACTS — the chain works end to end and this stage is genuinely reality-gated, not a bug wearing a blocker's clothes. Every CURRENT_PRE_EVENT forecast row since 08-22 carries market.noVig (verified per-row across the six most recent snapshots, 100% coverage), the grader writes market.scores from the forecast of record, and the ledger holds 8 graded / 3 paired — model logLoss 0.8733 vs market 0.8845 on the paired three, figures that support nothing at n=3 and are reported anyway per the rule above. The five unpaired rows are all forecasts of record from 08-21, generated before persistence landed: permanent gaps in OUR records, correctly excluded rather than scored. CAUTION FOR READERS OF THIS ENTRY: the 'Live: 1 graded, 0 paired' figure above is the P189 snapshot, and quoting it as current is exactly how the 08-24 operating record shipped '0 of 30 paired' while data/internal/research/epl/learning/latest.json (regenerated nightly inside epl-settle) said 3 — this entry records assessments at their dates; live counts live in the learning artifact." },
