      model: { status: "PROVEN", evidence: "Poisson score-matrix team model (epl-poisson / strength-state), cross-language parity with the live lib at n=1140 logLoss 1.0017, draw ECE 0.0262, totals diagnostics; lineups NOT_REQUIRED_FOR_TEAM_V1 by design (data/internal/research/epl/model-card-v1.json). PROVEN 2026-08-20: the prior text held this PARTIAL because \"all 10 matchweek-1 fixtures READY_EXCEPT_ODDS\" — true then, false now. 9 of 10 opening fixtures produce per-event distributions (e.g. Arsenal v Coventry City H 0.691 / D 0.178 / A 0.130); the tenth returns no market from the provider and is listed READY_EXCEPT_ODDS with its reason, never dropped. PREGAME INPUTS ONLY: the strength fit takes an explicit cutoff at the run clock so it can never see a result from a match it is forecasting, and odds are refused at/after kickoff. A newly promoted club with no top-flight history is FLAGGED coldStart rather than given a fabricated strength. The forecast set REFUSES to persist if any row claims CURRENT_PRE_EVENT while carrying no probabilities — the first build did exactly that, publishing nine rows that asserted a prediction and contained none. publicActivation stays OFF on every row: this proves the model RUNS, not that it should be acted on" },
